Q: Jenkins pipeline Workspace got deleted automatically A: <p>There is a default WS clean up strategy in Jenkins. The clean up thread will clean up all the old workspace in a regular cron job. You can check them in Manage Jenkins → Scripts Console by following commands.</p>
<pre><code>println &quot;disabled = ${hudson.model.WorkspaceCleanupThread.disabled}&quot;
println &quot;retainForDays = ${hudson.model.WorkspaceCleanupThread.retainForDays}&quot;
println &quot;recurrencePeriodHours = ${hudson.model.WorkspaceCleanupThread.recurrencePeriodHours}&quot;
</code></pre>
<p>Then you get something like:</p>
<pre><code>disabled = false
retainForDays = 30
recurrencePeriodHours = 24
</code></pre>
<p>Disabling it is a good solution as Sid mentioned. If you do not want to change the global setting, another solution would be to change the modify time of workspace in Jenkins job. So the CleanupThread won't consider it an old directory and delete it.</p>
<pre><code>stage('Build') {
    steps {
        sh '''
            touch &quot;$WORKSPACE&quot;
            stat &quot;$WORKSPACE&quot;
            ./build.sh
        '''
    }
}
</code></pre>
